  "scene_description": "Inside a cramped stone harbourmaster’s office at night, a mason in dusty work clothes stands beside a wooden desk, holding a freshly broken wedge of pale stone. Mortar clings beside the mason’s fingernails; their posture is tense and attentive. Across the desk, a tired harbourmaster with weathered features and pinned dark hair stands half risen from her chair, wearing a wool waistcoat, her fingers resting on a heavy iron key. A lantern lights an unfolded harbour chart, a closed ledger, and untouched bread. A wet coat drips onto a sack beside the wall. Through a small window, moored boats sit on dark, still harbour water. The atmosphere is intimate and apprehensive.",
